<p>Celebrated its 25th anniversary in 2016.</p>

<p>This beautiful yarn has a passionate cult following and deservedly so. At last count, it has been used in nearly 50,000 projects on Ravelry and is available in dozens of fabulous colorways!</p>

<p>“I imagined a yarn that bloomed out of a garden of silk and silk/mohair fabric,” says Mr. Eisaku Noro, its creator. We couldn’t agree more.</p>

<p>Gauge: 14-16 stitches, 22-24 rows</p>
', '10% Wool, 45% Silk, 45% Mohair', 'https://images4-f.ravelrycache.com/uploads/Jaydot/101135071/r-silkgarden_small.jpg', '{}'::jsonb, '2026-02-28T16:04:23.756634+00:00', '2026-02-28T16:04:23.756634+00:00'),
  (194, 'Kureyon（くれよん）', 'noro-kureyon', 'Noro', 15, 1, 'Aran', '10', '18', NULL, '8', 50, 109, NULL, NULL, '2 z-twisted singles z-plied together', 4, 14, 16, '7 ', '8 ', 4.5, 5, '8 ', '10.5', 5, 6.5, false, NULL, 4.2, 10884, 45740, '
<p>Kureyon has two plies. It can be a little difficult to see, because the yarn has such a “rustic” loosely spun effect, but if you untwist it you will definitely get two plies in your hand. It’s how they get the striated effect that shows up in some dye lots (like, black and orange blurred together.)</p>

<p>くれよん(pronounced coo-ray-oh-n) is the Japanese pronunciation of the English “crayon;” thus, the literal name of the yarn is “crayon.”</p>

<p>標準ゲージ (gauge): 14〜16 目(stitches), 22〜24 段(rows) <br />棒針 8〜10 号 (Japanese size; ~4.5mm - 5.1mm)</p>
', '100% Wool', 'https://images4-g.ravelrycache.com/flickr/1/5/6/15691861900/15691861900_m.jpg', '{}'::jsonb, '2026-02-28T16:04:19.513704+00:00', '2026-02-28T16:04:19.513704+00:00'),
